    <title>Any shape can ultimately cross information on two-dimensional abelian sandpile models</title>
    <updated>2017-08-04T20:47:26Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.00464v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1709.00464v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>In this paper we study the abelian sandpile model on the two-dimensional grid with uniform neighborhood, and prove that any family of neighborhoods defined as scalings of a continuous non-flat shape can ultimately perform crossing.</summary>
